Sat Nov 14 00:19:04 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add xawm-focus-explicit.patch: the traversal code defaulted to
  XawFocusPointer, so the EnterWindow/LeaveWindow translations of
  List, Command, Toggle, Repeater, Scrollbar, Panner and Text took the
  X input focus on enter and set it to PointerRoot on leave. Under a
  click-to-focus window manager the application then only received
  keys while the pointer was over it (Egon after the pointer crossed
  its object list). The default is now XawFocusExplicit, the Motif
  default; Tab traversal and FocusTake are unchanged

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 19:18:59 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add xawm-delete-key.patch: the default Text translations bound Delete and KP_Delete to delete-previous-character, so Delete erased backwards like BackSpace; they now delete the next character (Meta+Delete deletes the next word)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 16:53:20 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add xawm-xim-latin1.patch: 8-bit Text read keys with XLookupString,
  which does not compose dead keys (xedplus typed the bare accent).
  Keys now go through an XIM context on the shell window, shared with
  Mowitz, and come back as ISO 8859-1, also in the C locale

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 13:33:18 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Initial package of XawM 1.5u, the Motif-like Athena widget set
  used by Siag Office
- Add xawm-gcc15.patch: missing stdlib.h, prototypes for the Xt
  varargs internals and implicit int in the layout lexer/parser
- Add xawm-link-libs.patch: link libXawM against libXmu/Xt/Xext/X11
- Ship an X11/Xaw -> X11/XawM include symlink in /usr/include/XawM
  so <X11/Xaw/...> programs compile against the XawM structures
